[ERRORS label=place_add_order2] errors[] empty {DOC}
[ERRORS label=balance_after] errors[] empty {DOC}
[ERRORS label=history] errors[] empty {DOC}
[COUNT label=history] data.loyaltyPointsHistory.items[*?amount=@td(MSN_ORDERCOUNT.reward)].length = {{REWARD_COUNT_BEFORE}} + 1 {SPEC} — exactly one new Earned entry at this mission's reward amount. NOT pinned to the order: a mission-granted ledger entry carries object = null (measured live 2026-08-28 on the VIP fixture — all four known mission rewards 750/450/550/400 have a null object, while every product-earn entry carries type CustomerOrder + orderNumber), so .object.orderId cannot be asserted for a mission grant. Amount + count delta is the maximum the API permits; the missing attribution is BL-LOY-015.
[DATA label=history] data.loyaltyPointsHistory.items[?amount=@td(MSN_ORDERCOUNT.reward)].amount = @td(MSN_ORDERCOUNT.reward) {SPEC}
[DATA label=history] data.loyaltyPointsHistory.items[?amount=@td(MSN_ORDERCOUNT.reward)].object is null {OBSERVED} — recorded, not endorsed: a mission grant carries NO object, so it is attributable to neither a mission nor an order. Asserting the measured shape makes a future build that starts populating object fail this line loudly, at which point the case is upgraded to pin the order. It is the BL-LOY-015 violation made visible, not a behaviour anyone wants.

[ERRORS label=place_add_zeroreward] errors[] empty {DOC}
[ERRORS label=progress] errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA label=progress] data.loyaltyMissionProgress.items[?missionId=@td(MSN_ZEROREWARD.id)].status = Completed {SPEC}
[ERRORS label=balance_after] errors[] empty {DOC}
[ERRORS label=history_after] errors[] empty {DOC}
[COUNT label=history_after] data.loyaltyPointsHistory.items[*?amount=0].length = {{ZERO_AMOUNT_COUNT_BEFORE}} {SPEC} — narrowed 2026-08-28 from a whole-history total (which co-completing missions with NONZERO rewards can move without ZEROREWARD granting anything) to a count of amount=0 entries specifically. SCHEMA LIMITATION (confirmed via live introspection): the schema has no mission-identifying field on a history item, and the filter grammar cannot compound object.orderId with amount in one expression, so this is the closest available proxy for 'no entry attributable to this mission's zero-reward completion' — not a true per-order-and-mission attribution. A currentBalance=BAL_BEFORE equality was also dropped outright (not weakened to a relation): co-completing missions can add an UNBOUNDED, unpredictable amount to the balance on this env, so no valid relation on currentBalance exists for a zero-reward case at all.

[ERRORS label=place_add_dedup] errors[] empty {DOC}
[ERRORS label=history_1] errors[] empty {DOC}
[COUNT label=history_1] data.loyaltyPointsHistory.items[*?amount=@td(MSN_ORDERVALUE.reward)].length = {{AMOUNT_MATCH_COUNT_BEFORE}} + 1 {BL} — narrowed 2026-08-28 from the WHOLE Earned-history total (which a co-completing sibling mission — observed live on this account: LOCALIZED/ZEROTARGET/PUBLISHED_PRIVATE/ZEROREWARD can all settle on one order — legitimately also grows) to the count of entries carrying THIS mission's own reward amount (500), which does not collide with the observed co-completing set (250/200/100/0)
[ERRORS label=history_2] errors[] empty {DOC}
[COUNT label=history_2] data.loyaltyPointsHistory.items[*?amount=@td(MSN_ORDERVALUE.reward)].length = {{AMOUNT_MATCH_COUNT_BEFORE}} + 1 {BL} — the dedup check: unchanged from history_1's count on the SECOND read, same narrowed slice

